# GitHub language statistics (github-linguist)
#
# 1. Linguist classifies a top-level `examples/` directory as documentation and
#    leaves it out of the language bar. That folder is the point of this
#    repository -- 126 runnable examples across 13 languages -- so opt it back
#    in. Without this, GitHub reports "Python 100%", counting only scripts/
#    and coding-challenges/.
examples/** -linguist-documentation

# 2. Linguist types SQL as `data`, not `programming`, so it is excluded from
#    stats even once the rule above applies. These are hand-written teaching
#    queries, so mark them detectable.
*.sql linguist-detectable

# 3. The PDFs are build output of scripts/build_pdfs.py, not authored source.
resources/pdf/** linguist-generated
